winewayland: capture the round-17..37 client-surface / present-path work.

⛔ THIS IS A CAPTURE, NOT A SHIPPING DECISION. It lives in patches/unverified/, which
build.sh does NOT read. Nothing changes until someone promotes it deliberately (see
PROMOTION below).

WHY IT EXISTS. On 2026-07-31 the SHIPPED 11.10-21 winewayland.so was compared against the dev
build tree and found to contain NONE of this work -- verified on the release binary with a
positive control (335 vs 151 `wayland` strings, so both reads were real):

    feature                                    dev   shipped 11.10-21
    NEUTRON_NATIVE_STACK (win32 z -> wl stack)   1          0
    neutron_restack_apply                        1          0
    NEUTRON_TRACE / NT-EV per-present trace    1/7          0

An entire body of present-path engineering existed ONLY in ~/wine-tkg-git and was one
`git clean` from being lost. That is the LEAKY EXPORT failure the project has been bitten by
repeatedly (see wiki HOME.md), and this patch closes it.

WHAT IT CARRIES (7 files, 35 hunks, ~1690 lines, all inside dlls/winewayland.drv):
  * round-34 ABBA LOCK-ORDER FIX -- a real deadlock. wayland_client_surface_update() runs on
    every vkQueuePresentKHR and took win_data_mutex, then called user-lock functions inside it,
    while NtUserSetWindowPos held the user lock and waited on win_data_mutex. A present racing
    a SetWindowPos wedged both threads (toy-repro'd + eu-stack-proven). The inversion exists in
    STOCK upstream winewayland; games do not hit it (one swapchain, no window churn).
    ⇒ This alone is worth shipping.
  * round-35 NATIVE WIN32-Z-ORDER STACKING (`NEUTRON_NATIVE_STACK=1`) -- mirror the win32
    hierarchy in the wl_subsurface stack so natively-presenting client surfaces are ordered
    correctly instead of being suppressed.
  * round-36 temporal suppression (`NEUTRON_TEMPORAL`), round-37 broad tracing
    (`NEUTRON_TRACE`, the NT-EV per-present lines).
  * round-17/18/21 suppress-set history: the `attach(NULL)` path that DESTROYS a subsurface and
    orphans the wl_surface (present-wait then blocks forever -> DXVK CS backs up -> main thread
    deadlocks), and the place-below alternative that avoids it.
  * NEUTRON_WL_KEEPCLIENT (added 2026-07-31) -- do not destroy a client subsurface for a window
    that is transiently invisible under a VISIBLE parent. Measured on After Effects: 373 of ~630
    presents/session took the destructive branch. NOTE: this did NOT fix AE's blank composition
    (see OPEN_ISSUES) and its parent-visible discriminator is too narrow -- 4-6 presents still
    destroy the surface. Captured as-is; do not mistake it for a finished fix.

GATES: every behaviour change is env-gated and OFF by default --
  NEUTRON_NATIVE_STACK, NEUTRON_TEMPORAL, NEUTRON_TRACE, NEUTRON_WL_KEEPCLIENT,
  NEUTRON_DCOMP_SUPPRESS_CLIENT, NEUTRON_WL_DIAG, NEUTRON_GDIPATH, NEUTRON_PM_FULLCOPY,
  NEUTRON_RPC, NEUTRON_PROBE_X/Y.
⚠️ "Env-gated" is a CLAIM UNTIL MEASURED. The round-34 lock-order fix in particular is
structural and always-on by design. Verify default behaviour behaviourally before promoting.

VERIFIED: generated against the PATCH-BUILT baseline (_work, all 54 patches applied) -- never by
filtering a dev-tree diff, which is the trap that cost three builds. Applied to a pristine copy
of that baseline it reproduces all 7 dev-tree files BYTE-IDENTICALLY (cmp clean), i.e. it
rebuilds exactly the code that ran in every experiment this session.

PROMOTION (do all of it, in order):
  1. move to patches/ and run preserved-fixes/harnesses/check-patch-order.py;
  2. cut a runtime and confirm it BUILDS (it touches unixlib.h/waylanddrv.h -- ABI surface);
  3. smoke-test Premiere, Photoshop, Lightroom AND After Effects with every gate UNSET, and
     confirm no behaviour change vs the previous runtime. The suite currently works without
     this; regressing it would be a bad trade for code whose only proven win is a deadlock
     that does not reproduce on demand.

